{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/261816-i-ve-considered-submitting-material-to-onyx-path","id":261816,"title":"I've considered submitting material to Onyx Path","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-20T21:58:26-07:00","id":261816,"title":"I've considered submitting material to Onyx Path","content":"So, I'm working on my V20 idea titled <i>Richmond By Night</i>, the intro of which is posted over on the VTM forums, and after reading the guidelines for submissions and reading the disclosure form and style guide, I'm actually considering creating and then submitting material to Onyx Path for Vampire: The Masquerade (as it is the game I am most familiar with) instead of doing an open forum thread. I will do my best to conform to these standards as well as the current setting and themes of V20 so it can be worthy of submission (in other words, no homebrewing like I did with other projects).<br /> <br /> I have several vague ideas, the most developed is <i>Richmond By Night</i>, but from what I understand, the old &quot;X By Night&quot; books that White Wolf did tended to sell poorly and I'm unsure if that would be worthy of submission. That being said, there are some concepts and characters from this Richmond concept that I would love to submit to Onyx Path and hopefully see what sticks.<br /> <br /> What I want to know is what kind of Classic World of Darkness material is Onyx Path interested in? Any tips on making good material for submission? I think it would be a crowning moment of awesome for me if Onyx Path actually accepted one of my submissions, but even if it gets rejected, at least I know I tried my best and that it got read, which is good enough for me. And I would love to keep developing ideas, refine my ideas as a writer, and do my best. Hopefully I can come up with something that sticks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T22:48:36-07:00","id":261850,"title":"","content":"Okay, I know you probably really don't want to hear this, but it must be said.<br /> <br /> Cam, considering the number of problems you've had with both oWoD and nWoD's setting and themes and things like personal tragedy and stuff, are you really sure you'd <i>want</i> to write for Onyx Path?<br /> <br /> As for submissions, they aren't looking for anything innovative per se. They want to know how well you can handle fiction as well as mechanics. Odds are that whatever you write won't be used, it just has to illustrate your comprehension and ability to write compelling fiction and solid mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T23:48:37-07:00","id":261864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/261816-i-ve-considered-submitting-material-to-onyx-path?p=261850#post261850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I know you probably really don't want to hear this, but it must be said.<br /> <br /> Cam, considering the number of problems you've had with both oWoD and nWoD's setting and themes and things like personal tragedy and stuff, are you really sure you'd <i>want</i> to write for Onyx Path?<br /> <br /> As for submissions, they aren't looking for anything innovative per se. They want to know how well you can handle fiction as well as mechanics. Odds are that whatever you write won't be used, it just has to illustrate your comprehension and ability to write compelling fiction and solid mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point, but I have softened my attitude towards personal tragedy a lot in the past few months. But I do see your point on comprehension when it comes to submissions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T05:55:11-07:00","id":262081,"title":"","content":"Personally, myself I would love such a job like freelance writer, but:<br /> <br /> 1) Not sure about my actual skills (but I joined non-WoD RP forum that demands quality, so I will improve). I will take it step by step, and if I actually will be able to write major homebrews in a decent way maybe it would not be farfetched to picture myself as a freelance writer.<br /> <br /> 2) My prime field is actually translation. In 2 years I plan to take an exam for future sworn translators, so I will polish my translation skills and maybe if I find room outside my work as a legal translator and Onyx needs services of a Polish-to-English or English-to-Polish translator, I can help out with anything related to my native language.<br /> <br /> Actually, if an individual user needs some short amateur translation to be done, I can do it for free since I would welcome any occassion to practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T06:03:49-07:00","id":262084,"title":"","content":"I think I'd focus on the fiction...the story first and foremost.<br /> <br /> <br /> ..The only time I really felt compelled to write anything was for Palladium's Rifts. And not once did I consider game mechanics since it was a novel. The game was used simply as a guideline. And the one time I posted the first few chapters, I received a good deal of interest, with one person wanting to buy the book then and there. (a pity my personal life has squashed my time)<br /> <br /> But my experience is limited. and I've not tried to write anything for here. (and since I'm a reader and not a player)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T11:54:46-07:00","id":262332,"title":"","content":"I don't know if you've come across the writer all-call announcement from February, but these might be helpful if you haven't:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/do-you-want-to-walk-the-onyx-path/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/do-you-want-t...the-onyx-path/</a><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/writer-all-call-follow-up/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/writer-all-call-follow-up/\" target=\"_blank\"> Writer All-Call: Follow Up &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/writer-all-call-follow-up/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/writer-all-call-follow-up/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The all-call was almost half a year ago, so it might not be valid anymore (for all I know). But even if that particular avenue is closed, those are both good guidelines if you're serious about submitting a writing sample, especially the second link.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T12:13:45-07:00","id":262362,"title":"","content":"The all-call announcement says 1,000 words total; the submission guidelines say 1,000 of setting text and 1,000 of mechanics. I'm not sure which one to go with right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}